{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.reeb_moved_state_admits_chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.reeb_moved_state_admits_chirality","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L219-L226","doc":"Conversely, a state the involution **moves** admits such a bit — so the\nmechanism is not vacuous, it is exactly a fermion/boson dichotomy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.no_chirality_on_reeb_fixed_state","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.no_chirality_on_reeb_fixed_state","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L198-L217","doc":"**`archimedean-chirality.md`'s boson clause, as a theorem.**\n\nChirality is the `±`-eigenvalue of the Reeb involution `ξ ↦ −ξ`, i.e. a bit that\nis **odd** under it.  A purely horizontal object is one the involution fixes.\nNo such object can carry the bit: oddness would force `chir s = !chir s`.\n\nThis is `archimedean-chirality`'s \"bosons, being purely horizontal, are\nchirality-blind\" — and it is structurally the same argument as\n`LeptonNumberCarrierChirality.no_lepton_number_on_amphichiral_carrier`, one\nlevel up: a grading that anticommutes with an involution vanishes on its fixed\npoints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.flavour_and_chirality_alone_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.flavour_and_chirality_alone_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L189-L194","doc":"Likewise the particle bit: without it `u_L` and `ū_L` collide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.flavour_and_particle_alone_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.flavour_and_particle_alone_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L176-L187","doc":"**Each of the three bits is load-bearing: drop the chirality bit and the\nsector collapses.**\n\n`u_L` and `u_R` agree on flavour and on particle-ness, so without the chirality\nbit they are the same state.  This is the V9 claim in its sharpest form — the\nchirality datum is not decoration, it is required for the labelling to be\nfaithful. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.braid_element_cannot_separate_gen1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.braid_element_cannot_separate_gen1","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L157-L174","doc":"**One bit cannot separate the sector.**\n\nThe braid element supplies a single binary datum (the crossing sign).  No map\nout of `Bool` can be injective on eight states, so **at least two further\nindependent bits** are needed beyond the braid element — one of which the Reeb\ninvolution supplies, the other being the unformalized colour-tube environment\nlabel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.gen1_states_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.gen1_states_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L153-L155","doc":"The sector really does have eight pairwise-distinct states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.gen1_determined_by_flavour_chirality_particle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.gen1_determined_by_flavour_chirality_particle","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L144-L151","doc":"**The three bits determine the sector.**\n\nSo the labelling is exactly right-sized: three independent binary labels, eight\nstates, and the map to `Bool × Bool × Bool` is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.isParticle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.isParticle","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L139-L142","doc":"Particle bit: `true` = particle (not antiparticle). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.chirality","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L134-L137","doc":"Chirality bit: `true` = left-handed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.flavour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.flavour","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L129-L132","doc":"Flavour bit: `true` = up-type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.instDecidableEqGen1Quark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.instDecidableEqGen1Quark","kind":"instance","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.dRbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.dRbar","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.dLbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.dLbar","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.uRbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.uRbar","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.uLbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.uLbar","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.dR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.dR","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.dL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.dL","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.uR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.uR","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.uL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark.uL","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.Gen1Quark","kind":"inductive","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L121-L125","doc":"The eight first-generation quark states: flavour × chirality × particle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.chirality_not_a_function_of_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.chirality_not_a_function_of_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityIndependentOfCrossing.lean#L97-L117","doc":"**A chirality bit cannot be a function of the crossing sign.**\n\n`u_L` and `u_R` are both up quarks, so by the knot-particle dictionary they\ncarry the *same* braid element `σᵢ` and hence the same crossing sign; but they\nhave opposite chirality by definition.  Any `chir` factoring through `crossing`\nis therefore forced to give one value to both.\n\nThe hypotheses are exactly the corpus's own assignments: `h_up_same_crossing`\nis the dictionary row for `𝔲`, and `h_uL` / `h_uR` are the definitions of the\ntwo chiralities. ","signatureChunk":0}]}